      "id": 67336,
      "name": "Ironic",
      "username": "Ironic",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-07-08T07:49:33.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Blade sr. might have been involved, as a young man... or perhaps even&nbsp;<em>his</em> father. &nbsp;La Capitan can show up anywhen - indeed, she seems to have recruited Chip from around that time. &nbsp;(And, of course, other could use time travel, too, if needed.) &nbsp;The first big boom of UFO sighting happened during the war - what if Voss (a precocious young genetically-engineer juggernaught at age twelve) staged an invasion, but was beaten back and went to harrass another galaxy for a few decades to gain strength?</p><p>On the hero side, there are the time-travellers, again, Legacy, Bunker, Scholar, Haka and not-Adept seem like the only really logical calls thusfar.</p><p>For environments, Megalopolis still works fine in the past, Atlantis was still ruined, Insula Primalis has hardly changed in millions of years (40s heroes loved \"lost world\"settings even more than modern ones, really), Rook City mostly works, there's no exact date on when Anubis returned, and the Realm of Dischord is eternal. &nbsp;And, yet again, don't rule out time travel.</p><p>I really like the idea for time-appropriate promos, here. &nbsp;And maybe a \"Beaches Of Normandy\" or \"Meapolis World's Fair, 1939\" environment deck.</p>",
